    "result_text": "The test passes. \n\n## Summary\n\nThe change request \u2014 \"show me how many projects and contacts a client has\" \u2014 is implemented as a single new additive file:\n\n**`src/main/frontend/features/clients/counts.slot.tsx`**\n\nIt fills the existing `ClientDetail` slot region (CLAUDE.md rule 3) on the client detail page with an at-a-glance count of projects and contacts, exposing `data-testid=\"client-projects-count\"` and `data-testid=\"client-contacts-count\"`.\n\nNo schema, server, or existing-file changes were needed: the app already exposes `/api/clients/{id}/projects` and `/api/clients/{id}/contacts`. Per CLAUDE.md rule 5, the slot queries under the *same* nested keys the projects/contacts tables use (`['clients', id, 'projects']` and `['clients', id, 'contacts']`) and renders `.length`, so the counts stay in step with those tables through the shared key \u2014 no imports between features beyond the shared query helpers, and any write that invalidates `['clients']` refreshes the numbers automatically.\n\nFrontend typecheck passes and the Playwright acceptance test passes (projects count `2`, contacts count `3`).",
